    "lawCode": "Amd §3-0309, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3442\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\nguidelines for disqualifying stand-by contractors\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nAuthorizes the department of environmental conservation to promulgate\nguidelines for the disqualification of stand-by contractors authorized\nunder environmental conservation law 3-0309.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nAuthorizes establishing guidelines for disqualification of stand-by\ncontractors based upon past performance, reasonableness of price\ncharged, acts of negligence or malfeasance, and convictions of certain\ncrimes.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nCurrent law authorizes guidelines for qualifying stand-by contractors\nbut not disqualifying them. State finance law terms for\ndisqualification are woefully inadequate for addressing the potential\ndisqualification of stand-by contractors for environmental concerns.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n1997-98: A.1372 Passed Assembly\n1999: A.547 Passed Assembly\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\n120 days after the act becomes law.\n",
